      "message": "Hi jpawlowski@,\nI have C++ questions here, do we need `Unretained`? `Unretained` allows Bind() to bind a non-refcounted class, and to disable refcounting on arguments that are refcounted objects.\nI have two understandings here, and don\u0027t know which one is correct:\n1. `HearingAid::Get()` returns an `HearingAidImpl* instance`, which is a global variable. As a global variable, it is not a refcounted objects and needs `Unretained`?\n2. Or maybe it is okay to remove `Unretained` because with this change, because `Connect` becomes static and no longer needs a `HearingAidImpl* instance`?",
